# SQL's `NOT IN`: DS0105 with a fix to `!in`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT IN ('a', 'b')
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..55
  PIPELINE@0..54
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..54
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      IN_EXPR@26..54
        NAME_REF@26..36
          IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        IDENT@37..40 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
        IDENT@41..43 "IN"
        WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
        ARG_LIST@44..54
          L_PAREN@44..45 "("
          LITERAL@45..48
            STRING@45..48 "'a'"
          COMMA@48..49 ","
          WHITESPACE@49..50 " "
          LITERAL@50..53
            STRING@50..53 "'b'"
          R_PAREN@53..54 ")"
  WHITESPACE@54..55 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `NOT IN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT IN ('a', 'b')
  |                                      ^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: write `!in` to test that a value is not in a list

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where customerId !in ('a', 'b')
which parses without errors
